  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)=-\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$",
  "worked_solution": "The given equation is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u20613x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{18}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=-\\frac{1}{18}.$",
